 ⍙R←⍙TEMPPATH ⍙COMMAND ⍙CMD;⍙PATH;⍙T;⍙TFILE
⍝ Utility function for executing a Windows command and returning the
⍝ result as a character vector.  This utility creates a temporary text
⍝ file in the given ⍙TEMPPATH and removes it when it is done working.

⍝ Used like:
⍝   ⍙R←'C:\temp\' ⍙COMMAND 'C:\path\' 'fc "C:\path\filename.txt" "C:\path\filename.txt"'

 (⍙PATH ⍙CMD)←⍙CMD ⍝ Path to execute in and command to execute
:If 0≠⍴⍙PATH ⋄ ⍝ Set execution directory if passed
  :if '\'=⍙T←⎕FIRST ⍙PATH ⋄ ⍙T←'' ⋄ :endif
   ⍙T←⍙T ⎕CHDIR ⍙PATH ⍝ Change DOS directory
:EndIf
⍝ Include trailing delim if needed:
:if ~∨/(¯1↑⍙TEMPPATH)='\/' ⋄ ⍙TEMPPATH←⍙TEMPPATH,'\' ⋄ :endif
 ⍙TFILE←⍙TEMPPATH,'APLCOMMANDTEMPFILE.txt'
 3 ⎕CMD ⍙CMD,' >> ',⍙TFILE,' 2>&1' ⍝ Execute command and create the temp file
⍝ Read the resulting text output:
 ⍙T←⎕XNNUMS,⎕NNUMS ⋄ ⍙T←-((⍳⍴⍙T)∊∣⍙T)⍳0 ⍝ Find a tie
 ⍙TFILE ⎕XNTIE ⍙T ⍝ Tie text file
 ⍙R←⎕NREAD ⍙T 82 (⎕NSIZE ⍙T) 0 ⍝ Read all of it
⍝ Delete the text file now we have read it:
 ⍙TFILE ⎕XNERASE ⍙T